  "summary_en": "Kenya's 2026 national policy framework for governing AI and other emerging technologies, including robotics and autonomous systems as 'scaling technologies'. It sets nine pillars, a risk-based lifecycle approach, an AI Council and Office, human oversight and transparency principles, and an implementation and M&E matrix. Embodied AI is only mentioned in passing.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Risk-based, lifecycle approach with stricter obligations for high-risk systems",
   "Creates a National AI and Emerging Technologies Council and Office for coordination",
   "Meaningful human control, including limits and interrupt ability for agentic systems",
   "Disclosure when AI interacts with or decides about individuals; rights to review and redress",
   "Legacy systems get 2-year transition (3 years for high-risk); robotics listed as emerging technology with regulatory gaps"
  ],
